        {
          "id": "UgxFNJeIhe5rm-7gzhF4AaABAg",
          "author_name": "@jasonholmes6543",
          "author_url": "http://www.youtube.com/@jasonholmes6543",
          "text": "Doesn’t vibe coding mean you either don’t care about the code or you can’t understand the code. Either way its mass produced slop, right?\n\nMy point is using LLMs to assist decision making (provided you haven’t completely abdicated your own responsibility to understand WTF you are talking about) is not vibe coding.",
          "like_count": 2,
          "reply_count": 2,
          "published_at": "2026-04-29T03:02:28Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-29T03:02:51Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgwPntveSQ-F93cT6zR4AaABAg",
          "author_name": "@elendal",
          "author_url": "http://www.youtube.com/@elendal",
          "text": "Hmm, I've tried one of Steve Yegge's AI coded apps, it run for 40.0s, I've optimized it to run in 4 (gastownhall/beads/issues/3520). Pretty sure this would not happen had he used his own intelligence. His app that supposed to replace jira, is already slower than Jira with only 200 issues recorded.",
          "like_count": 2,
          "reply_count": 3,
          "published_at": "2026-04-28T20:23:04Z",
          "updated_at": "2026-04-28T20:35:46Z"
        },
        {
          "id": "UgyN0J3Sdbuy9_D172R4AaABAg",
          "author_name": "@countvoncount42",
          "author_url": "http://www.youtube.com/@countvoncount42",
          "text": "\"Enterprise rigor\". That's exactly my kind of humor! 😂 \"Rigor mortis\" most of the time, tho.",
